---
title: "merkle_tree::is_proof_valid (Pyth Sui Contracts)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_leaf: current_digest = leaf_hash(leaf_data)
    q_leaf --> q_size: proofSize = deserialize_u8(encoded_proof)
    q_size --> q_loop: proofSize > 0
    q_loop --> q_sibling: true
    q_loop --> q_compare: false
    q_sibling --> q_node: sibling_digest = bytes20::new(deserialize_vector(proof, 20))
    q_node --> q_dec: current_digest = node_hash(current_digest, sibling_digest)
    q_dec --> q_loop: proofSize = proofSize - 1
    q_compare --> [*]: return data(current_digest) == data(root)

    note right of q_node
        INV-001: node_hash sorts children before hashing (canonical ordering)
        INV-002: leaf_hash uses MERKLE_LEAF_PREFIX (0) as domain separator
        INV-003: node_hash uses MERKLE_NODE_PREFIX (1) as domain separator
        INV-004: hash output is truncated to 20 bytes (keccak256 leftmost 20)
    end note
